(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.991926804981785*^9, 
  3.991926806092729*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"feb885f2-bc38-4107-84e2-\
c4275c110672"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Given this system for metrics: \
https://github.com/richzhang/PerceptualSimilarity what do you think wwould be \
a good way to use it from within WL? A python link or re-implementation in WL?\
\>", "ChatInput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "ChatNotebookSettings" -> <|
    "Model" -> <|"Service" -> "LLMKit", "Name" -> Automatic|>, "LLMEvaluator" -> 
     "WolframAIAssistant"|>|>,
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2710ee49-2511-489f-b9c9-1c80ccc7fa28"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell["PerceptualSimilarity", Background -> None]},
   "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
  "62568b84-f54e-44a5-8468-c2d3135c57a7"],
 " specifically, I would strongly recommend ",
 StyleBox["using it from Wolfram Language through Python rather than \
reimplementing it in pure WL",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ". \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Why Python link is the better choice\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}},
   ScrollPosition->{0., 0.}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"3bd69957-1202-4f2f-90e0-08c4e8060bf8"],
 "\nThat repository is built around: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "PyTorch"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"b5982caf-b976-486f-bb76-54c558463ad9"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "pretrained network weights"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"6a98ca0b-4308-47ea-bdae-7a442a085173"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "image preprocessing conventions tied to the original implementation"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"594c14bb-e702-4ebc-80de-5bee56bd5497"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "GPU support through the Python deep learning stack"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"518043f9-e2e9-4453-a786-2402d96aeb10"],
 "\nA WL reimplementation would be possible in principle, but in practice it \
would likely be: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "a lot of work"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"8ebcc629-8119-4891-bb57-8b38fe26056c"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "hard to validate against the reference implementation"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"cc1fde7d-a0b2-437c-9b23-d5b6e26be7b9"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "fragile if the upstream project changes"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"92de83a9-cc7f-47bb-80b9-9fb7d2a01ceb"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "potentially slower to get working, especially with GPU support"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"9d738f70-4ab0-46ff-8a50-4c7f728c9234"],
 "\nIf your goal is ",
 StyleBox["use the metric reliably",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", then the best architecture is:\n\n1. keep the official Python \
implementation as the source of truth\n2. call it from WL\n3. convert \
images/results back into native WL objects \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Best integration options in WL\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"dec2f2ac-8cff-4ee9-9cc4-3b9a13cdbdc7"],
 "\nThere are really two sensible approaches. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox[Cell[TextData[{
     "1. ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      TemplateBox[{
       "ExternalEvaluate", "paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate", 
        "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/ExternalEvaluate.html"},
       "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"1e8459bd-188b-481b-816e-889e87f1c431"],
     " / Python session"
    }],
     Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"264303e0-ecbb-402e-9d2f-3ffb549873a3"],
     "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"044d6218-babd-422d-ab0c-67672765ebbb"],
 "\nThis is the most natural interactive solution from inside notebooks.\n\n\
You can start a Python session with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"StartExternalSession", "[", "\"\<Python\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineWL", 
  "Input",
  ShowAutoStyles->True,
  ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
  LanguageCategory->"Input",
  ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
  "c9288680-a1d3-467a-a16c-3c599fcfaed4"],
 " and call Python code using ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
   "ExternalEvaluate", "paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate", 
    "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/ExternalEvaluate.html"},
   "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"0f429c39-991a-4154-80ee-b6e85bfd2777"],
 ". This is the simplest way to: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "load the LPIPS model once"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"4a5f9415-fe09-48d7-b534-4e0fe63f1d69"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "keep it in memory"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"8fbc5dd3-61c1-4299-bc37-548cce51295a"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "send images or file paths from WL"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"141b1e6c-22d8-4784-9ade-de0357347164"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "get back scalar distances or arrays"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"4cff232a-f41f-4ef9-a1c5-4c9378e60b2f"],
 "\nThis is probably the ",
 StyleBox["best choice for exploration and notebook workflows",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ".\n\nThe documented pattern is exactly this kind of usage: create a Python \
session, evaluate Python code, and optionally return Wolfram expressions via \
the Wolfram Client Library for Python using ",
 StyleBox["wl", "TI"],
 ". See the docs for the Python external evaluation system and the Wolfram \
Client Library for Python expression representation. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"2. A small Python wrapper script/service\"\>", "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"805c13bc-f8c1-423e-9923-1c63b0f97744"],
 "\nIf you want something more production-like, make a thin Python wrapper \
around the repo and call it from WL.\n\nFor example, WL could: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "export two images to temp files"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"6626d0dd-80c4-47f3-bc89-e8919ac08998"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "run a Python script that computes LPIPS"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"27c1f445-5f79-476d-8bbd-761552a2dcce"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "read back JSON/text output"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"e500b02e-3edb-4d66-989d-0573f2347299"],
 "\nThis is often more robust than embedding lots of Python source strings \
inside WL, especially if: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "you need environment management"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"7cfa9e2e-5221-4f87-a2ae-26f3048577d2"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "you want reproducibility"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"b8c48660-f35f-485c-a863-5d8daa129d88"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "multiple users/machines are involved"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"c45e4a3e-1e32-4d8d-a636-52521cb8e047"],
 "\nThis is probably the ",
 StyleBox["best choice for automation or deployment",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ". \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"When a WL reimplementation might make sense\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"d32a45a0-01e9-4e89-820b-29b0910197f7"],
 "\nA reimplementation in WL is only worth considering if one of these is \
true: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "you want a ",
  StyleBox["research/educational",
   FontWeight->Bold],
  " implementation"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"920d763c-2239-4d64-8774-f9d50cd2ce59"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "you only need an ",
  StyleBox["approximation",
   FontWeight->Bold],
  " of the metric"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"7c819d2f-b03b-4cde-8dea-e72a393ff00a"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "you want tight integration with WL neural net tooling"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"44f81315-f215-4b13-9973-c9c2082f13d9"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "you want to modify the architecture in ways better expressed in WL"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"59a4dffd-3c7f-4a66-a3d3-7d6cc976fed2"],
 "\nBut if you need compatibility with the published LPIPS behavior, \
reimplementation is risky. The exact result depends on more than just the \
nominal architecture: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "channel normalization"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"f59d689f-5723-413a-8874-c6ce773d3e0a"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "resizing rules"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"1d45e912-04b0-4135-b3b1-725e98a0b9ba"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "layer selection"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"cf840cc7-ad48-4d9e-89a9-c4c7c5ae7ead"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "feature scaling"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"604431f7-41ca-4f23-a541-89722a47468d"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "learned linear calibration weights"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"967053f3-7667-4f87-972b-9e5ae5a1cada"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "model checkpoint details"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"a888cb2c-358a-4706-a201-0f6bfa605ca4"],
 "\nGetting all of that exactly right is the hard part. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"My recommendation\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"f3d383de-05ad-4e0e-ac36-56dc320a325d"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Recommended path\"\>", "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"216c0957-5643-4dbb-94de-559e63b9fb93"],
 "\nUse a ",
 StyleBox["Python-backed WL interface",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ".\n\nConcretely: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "install the repo in a Python environment"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"11813ad9-7a6e-4b25-9e63-eae02b807366"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "access it from WL through ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
    "ExternalEvaluate", "paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate", 
     "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/ExternalEvaluate.html"},
    "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"d9ebdcb2-2d6b-4b16-999e-195192cd03a6"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"c3435935-dfe3-4ff0-805d-09ba7b3b3987"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "pass image filenames or raw arrays"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"86a34283-4021-43d6-9884-550f4418b418"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "return numeric scores to WL"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"4c19aabc-6364-46bb-84c9-2a5342417b28"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Practical design\"\>", "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"05f8c946-f1fc-4c41-b6aa-08dd7abd4a4c"],
 "\nI would structure it as: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  StyleBox["WL side",
   FontWeight->Bold],
  ": user-facing function like ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell["lpipsDistance[img1_, img2_, opts___]", Background -> None]},
    "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
   "35aa70d7-7383-4de4-b581-5454e685a125"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"c5341f16-2274-47c3-a36b-dc3e094eea91"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  StyleBox["Python side",
   FontWeight->Bold],
  ": persistent session with model cached"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"1251eaa4-022b-4bbe-830e-5c89ec999355"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  StyleBox["Communication",
   FontWeight->Bold],
  ": preferably file paths first, then array transfer only if needed"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"967af8d0-3427-4288-a2c3-cb0dcaefb1e0"],
 "\nUsing file paths is often the easiest because it avoids headaches around: \
\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "color channel order"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"445ea52d-aa5a-4b59-99ad-39d2c5355b53"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "numeric dtype"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"4e0aa1be-981d-4303-bab4-a3c08c346052"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "tensor shape conventions"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"72ca002a-69e9-4a9e-b633-c9df01711ebb"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "serialization overhead"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"609a30f0-c4e2-47f1-9517-e46f9bbedfa7"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Suggested architecture\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"1bab115a-a7f0-43db-a0f4-d86db908d973"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Option A: persistent Python session in WL\"\>", "Subsection",
    
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"a69f5052-1974-4c74-b788-a1698e4500ca"],
 "\nGood for notebook use.\n\nWL wrapper roughly does: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"session", "=", 
            RowBox[{"StartExternalSession", "[", "\"Python\"", "]"}]}], ";"}],
         "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
        RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", 
          
          RowBox[{"session", ",", 
            "\"\nimport lpips\nloss_fn = lpips.LPIPS(net='alex')\n\""}], 
          "]"}]}]], "ChatCode", "Input", LanguageCategory -> "Input", 
     ShowAutoStyles -> True, ShowStringCharacters -> True, ShowSyntaxStyles -> 
     True, TranslationOptions -> {"Enabled" -> Dynamic[
         AbsoluteCurrentValue[$FrontEnd, {TranslationOptions, "Enabled"}]]}], 
    "Wolfram"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "8a226d93-33a1-4ae8-828f-d3c2158b1b47"],
 "\nThen each call exports images and asks Python for the score. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Option B: command-line bridge\"\>", "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"2b3cbcf8-c46c-431e-b32b-652fa0ffb260"],
 "\nGood for stable pipelines. \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "write ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell["compute_lpips.py", Background -> None]},
    "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
   "c73e976e-efdf-4428-bebd-ed56e84eac79"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"5d26be99-13c8-4063-accb-a08a695bb346"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "WL runs it on exported image files"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"5e2f5e23-5744-409d-8fdf-99f2ed031635"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "parse returned score"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"c26242cd-72a4-4fc3-806b-def3ae39d0c7"],
 "\nThis is easier to debug and less dependent on notebook session state. \n\
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Performance considerations\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"23b4e3b0-1a1b-4cdf-99df-5c0acc6bf434"],
 "\nPython will likely outperform a WL reimplementation here because: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "PyTorch is heavily optimized"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"76707795-7819-47f7-89a1-dbb2a8bad5b5"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "pretrained models are already available"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"df68ccc0-65e9-44c0-a52a-d3e5f953db61"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "GPU acceleration is straightforward"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"dcdb8177-87d4-4926-b607-61e41c80b510"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "no need to rebuild low-level tensor ops in WL"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"14903775-9a13-4f3d-a047-82284e38a091"],
 "\nA WL reimplementation might only be competitive if you already have the \
exact model imported as a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
   "NetGraph", "paclet:ref/NetGraph", 
    "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/NetGraph.html"},
   "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"02fbc689-ff63-4c18-9249-b60b6c37511c"],
 " or related neural net object and can faithfully reproduce the full \
pipeline. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Validation matters\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"7c5cab92-87ae-41b6-ab56-af25c341a746"],
 "\nEven if you do build a WL version, I would still first create a Python \
bridge and use it as a reference. Then you can compare: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "same input image pair"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"643d6b59-0fdf-4547-aa75-bc18849ebe2b"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "Python LPIPS score"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"9e50e5f7-9a8b-4fb7-b45e-3d6af318e2cf"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "WL LPIPS score"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"b5a870d3-4a7a-4833-9184-02f4765ecdfb"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "numerical tolerance across test cases"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"8947902c-4575-4a5d-8bf6-910d10270964"],
 "\nWithout that, it is hard to trust the reimplementation. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Bottom line\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"fd0f8fc2-c346-4cb7-a5d8-18936d0430ac"],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["Use Python integration, not a full WL reimplementation.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "For interactive work: use ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
    "ExternalEvaluate", "paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate", 
     "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/ExternalEvaluate.html"},
    "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"dcd384c9-acd2-486a-8e9a-d4b455ca6a7b"],
  " with a persistent Python session."
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"1927accd-cc63-40e1-8517-b764b2acc854"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "For robust workflows: use a small Python wrapper script called from WL."
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"13b5e257-1907-40ac-b499-d7082a45c26e"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "Only reimplement in WL if your goal is methodological exploration rather \
than faithful use of the published metric."
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"fcf62f88-f4fb-40bb-83d8-1b95867d15ee"],
 "\nIf you want, I can sketch a clean WL wrapper around the Python LPIPS \
package, either using:\n1. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
   "ExternalEvaluate", "paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate", 
    "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/ExternalEvaluate.html"},
   "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"44bb5f68-33b7-478f-a762-5bb78bf30e91"],
 ", or\n2. a standalone Python script plus WL function."
}], "ChatOutput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "For ``PerceptualSimilarity`` specifically, I would strongly recommend \
**using it from Wolfram Language through Python rather than reimplementing it \
in pure WL**.\n\n## Why Python link is the better choice\n\nThat repository \
is built around:\n\n- PyTorch\n- pretrained network weights\n- image \
preprocessing conventions tied to the original implementation\n- GPU support \
through the Python deep learning stack\n\nA WL reimplementation would be \
possible in principle, but in practice it would likely be:\n\n- a lot of work\
\n- hard to validate against the reference implementation\n- fragile if the \
upstream project changes\n- potentially slower to get working, especially \
with GPU support\n\nIf your goal is **use the metric reliably**, then the \
best architecture is:\n\n1. keep the official Python implementation as the \
source of truth\n2. call it from WL\n3. convert images/results back into \
native WL objects\n\n## Best integration options in WL\n\nThere are really \
two sensible approaches.\n\n### 1. \
[ExternalEvaluate](paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate) / Python session\nThis is the \
most natural interactive solution from inside notebooks.\n\nYou can start a \
Python session with ``StartExternalSession[\"Python\"]`` and call Python code \
using ``ExternalEvaluate``. This is the simplest way to:\n\n- load the LPIPS \
model once\n- keep it in memory\n- send images or file paths from WL\n- get \
back scalar distances or arrays\n\nThis is probably the **best choice for \
exploration and notebook workflows**.\n\nThe documented pattern is exactly \
this kind of usage: create a Python session, evaluate Python code, and \
optionally return Wolfram expressions via the Wolfram Client Library for \
Python using ``wl``. See the docs for the Python external evaluation system \
and the Wolfram Client Library for Python expression representation.\n\n### \
2. A small Python wrapper script/service\nIf you want something more \
production-like, make a thin Python wrapper around the repo and call it from \
WL.\n\nFor example, WL could:\n\n- export two images to temp files\n- run a \
Python script that computes LPIPS\n- read back JSON/text output\n\nThis is \
often more robust than embedding lots of Python source strings inside WL, \
especially if:\n\n- you need environment management\n- you want \
reproducibility\n- multiple users/machines are involved\n\nThis is probably \
the **best choice for automation or deployment**.\n\n## When a WL \
reimplementation might make sense\n\nA reimplementation in WL is only worth \
considering if one of these is true:\n\n- you want a **research/educational** \
implementation\n- you only need an **approximation** of the metric\n- you \
want tight integration with WL neural net tooling\n- you want to modify the \
architecture in ways better expressed in WL\n\nBut if you need compatibility \
with the published LPIPS behavior, reimplementation is risky. The exact \
result depends on more than just the nominal architecture:\n\n- channel \
normalization\n- resizing rules\n- layer selection\n- feature scaling\n- \
learned linear calibration weights\n- model checkpoint details\n\nGetting all \
of that exactly right is the hard part.\n\n## My recommendation\n\n### \
Recommended path\nUse a **Python-backed WL interface**.\n\nConcretely:\n\n- \
install the repo in a Python environment\n- access it from WL through \
[ExternalEvaluate](paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate)\n- pass image filenames or \
raw arrays\n- return numeric scores to WL\n\n### Practical design\nI would \
structure it as:\n\n- **WL side**: user-facing function like \
``lpipsDistance[img1_, img2_, opts___]``\n- **Python side**: persistent \
session with model cached\n- **Communication**: preferably file paths first, \
then array transfer only if needed\n\nUsing file paths is often the easiest \
because it avoids headaches around:\n\n- color channel order\n- numeric dtype\
\n- tensor shape conventions\n- serialization overhead\n\n## Suggested \
architecture\n\n### Option A: persistent Python session in WL\nGood for \
notebook use.\n\nWL wrapper roughly does:\n\n```wl\nsession = \
StartExternalSession[\"Python\"];\nExternalEvaluate[session, \"\nimport lpips\
\nloss_fn = lpips.LPIPS(net='alex')\n\"]\n```\n\nThen each call exports \
images and asks Python for the score.\n\n### Option B: command-line bridge\n\
Good for stable pipelines.\n\n- write ``compute_lpips.py``\n- WL runs it on \
exported image files\n- parse returned score\n\nThis is easier to debug and \
less dependent on notebook session state.\n\n## Performance considerations\n\n\
Python will likely outperform a WL reimplementation here because:\n\n- \
PyTorch is heavily optimized\n- pretrained models are already available\n- \
GPU acceleration is straightforward\n- no need to rebuild low-level tensor \
ops in WL\n\nA WL reimplementation might only be competitive if you already \
have the exact model imported as a [NetGraph](paclet:ref/NetGraph) or related \
neural net object and can faithfully reproduce the full pipeline.\n\n## \
Validation matters\n\nEven if you do build a WL version, I would still first \
create a Python bridge and use it as a reference. Then you can compare:\n\n- \
same input image pair\n- Python LPIPS score\n- WL LPIPS score\n- numerical \
tolerance across test cases\n\nWithout that, it is hard to trust the \
reimplementation.\n\n## Bottom line\n\n**Use Python integration, not a full \
WL reimplementation.**\n\n- For interactive work: use \
[ExternalEvaluate](paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate) with a persistent Python \
session.\n- For robust workflows: use a small Python wrapper script called \
from WL.\n- Only reimplement in WL if your goal is methodological exploration \
rather than faithful use of the published metric.\n\nIf you want, I can \
sketch a clean WL wrapper around the Python LPIPS package, either using:\n1. \
``ExternalEvaluate``, or\n2. a standalone Python script plus WL function.", 
   "ChatData" -> 
