Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
I've stepped away from this for a bit and want to pick it up again. I've been \
using uv for my python management, etc and  want to integrate some metric \
into here. \
\>", "ChatInput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "ChatNotebookSettings" -> <|
    "Model" -> <|"Service" -> "LLMKit", "Name" -> Automatic|>, "LLMEvaluator" -> 
     "WolframAIAssistant", "ServiceCaller" -> "Chatbar"|>|>,
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ed80aa19-0070-4649-91a2-2056b2f0def5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a good fit. If you\[CloseCurlyQuote]re already \
using ",
 StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
 ", I\[CloseCurlyQuote]d still suggest a ",
 StyleBox["Python-backed integration",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " from WL, with ",
 StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
 " managing the environment and dependencies. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Recommendation\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"462b1ee2-f02f-4c09-994f-893da3d7f503"],
 "\nUse: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
  " to create/manage a dedicated Python environment"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"168967b7-0374-4154-8def-d49510a6e387"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
    "ExternalEvaluate", "paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate", 
     "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/ExternalEvaluate.html"},
    "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"2e103f21-b9c7-414c-850b-54b7e3a4a4a5"],
  " or ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
    "StartExternalSession", "paclet:ref/StartExternalSession", 
     "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/StartExternalSession.html"},
    "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"fd96a413-d45c-49b6-8075-48f2002c642a"],
  " from WL"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"c365ef21-2b2c-4871-8968-6d3c6dba4070"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "a small WL wrapper that talks to that Python environment"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"277c1764-52e3-4ed7-9de6-4cf798a9c830"],
 "\nThis gives you: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "reproducible Python deps"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"baa540b5-935f-460e-b79d-5cf48507162e"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "access to PyTorch / LPIPS without reimplementation"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"b4892fc1-8206-4ef1-a8e6-df8bace2edbf"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "a clean WL-facing API"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"723d771d-30f1-4dd5-b565-55f9caa0a71f"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Two workable patterns\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"debc48af-1b01-40b3-af52-287738f62aae"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox[Cell[TextData[{
     "1. Point WL at a ",
     StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
     "-managed Python"
    }],
     Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"798a297f-fc90-4432-af9a-60122dd4d093"],
     "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"a74df1cf-6864-4c50-b865-930da5037293"],
 "\nThis is the simplest if your ",
 StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
 " environment already has everything installed.\n\nAt the WL side, you want \
Python configured so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
   "FindExternalEvaluators", "paclet:ref/FindExternalEvaluators", 
    "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/FindExternalEvaluators.html"},
   
   "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"bd3f9fab-5e92-4b8e-9d0c-0b03405af392"],
 " can see it, then use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
   "ExternalEvaluate", "paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate", 
    "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/ExternalEvaluate.html"},
   "TextRefLink"]],ExpressionUUID->"d554531d-ff3a-474d-bb90-30780402f17c"],
 ".\n\nTypical docs flow is: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "verify Python exists"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"51513804-c76e-4014-8fd0-f52db961e9e5"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "install needed packages"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"353326bd-6c61-4c1a-a765-70bbe0e58fbc"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "confirm with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   RowBox[{"FindExternalEvaluators", "[", "\"\<Python\>\"", "]"}]], 
   "InlineWL", "Input",
   ShowAutoStyles->True,
   ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
   LanguageCategory->"Input",
   ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
   "4aeabfc3-22b6-4309-b04d-deb85317172e"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"127796a5-617d-420a-96d7-15b4dd77a8b7"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "call ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Python\>\"", ",", "..."}], "]"}]], "InlineWL", "Input",
   ShowAutoStyles->True,
   ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
   LanguageCategory->"Input",
   ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
   "3957010f-a2a8-4497-8b42-c065bd1a05b2"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"0e6004cb-2e12-4c7f-9a5a-c99ff5119644"],
 "\nThe docs also support dependency-managed evaluators directly through: \n\
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", " ", 
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"\"Python\"", ",", 
              RowBox[{"\"Evaluator\"", "->", 
                RowBox[{"<|", 
                  RowBox[{"\"Dependencies\"", "->", 
                    RowBox[{"{", "\"numpy\"", "}"}]}], "|>"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
           "\[IndentingNewLine]", " ", 
          "\"import numpy; numpy.__version__\""}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
        "]"}]], "ChatCode", "Input", LanguageCategory -> "Input", 
     ShowAutoStyles -> True, ShowStringCharacters -> True, ShowSyntaxStyles -> 
     True, TranslationOptions -> {"Enabled" -> Dynamic[
         AbsoluteCurrentValue[$FrontEnd, {TranslationOptions, "Enabled"}]]}], 
    "Wolfram"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "54b9e9f9-1fd9-40df-b23b-6934496424c3"],
 "\nThat dependency mechanism is useful, but since you already use ",
 StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
 ", I would probably ",
 StyleBox["let uv own the environment",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", rather than split package management between WL and the external \
evaluator provisioner. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox[Cell[TextData[{
     "Best practical setup with ",
     StyleBox["uv", "TI"]
    }],
     Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"28bf787b-411d-4b66-a131-1ead56de658a"],
     "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"05946f2f-85c7-41e7-8691-f61a822b1804"],
 "\nI\[CloseCurlyQuote]d suggest a project-local environment dedicated to \
image metrics.\n\nFor example, outside WL: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      Cell[
      "uv venv .venv\nuv pip install torch torchvision lpips pillow", 
       "ExternalLanguage", CellEvaluationLanguage -> "Shell", FontSize -> 13, 
       Background -> None, CellFrame -> None]]], "Shell"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "9f70fcb5-a981-433b-9254-cacd3b0a0e31"],
 "\nThen identify the Python executable inside that environment, something \
like: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "macOS/Linux: ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[".venv/bin/python", Background -> None]},
    "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
   "8e0de789-e43c-4176-9e1d-fba5a7c96438"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"f039746e-7dbc-4a69-a05f-f6cbf1e16cf7"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "Windows: ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[".venv\\Scripts\\python.exe", Background -> None]},
    "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
   "b038743b-a842-4f0c-a1b9-658564767f80"]
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"ca360ba3-6faa-471b-88ea-4c1db9426f48"],
 "\nThen in WL, use that interpreter explicitly. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"How to connect WL to that Python\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"79af9373-a6f8-4fb9-ad0d-623f95d6099c"],
 "\nA good first step in WL is to start a session with that interpreter. \
Depending on your setup, this usually means configuring Python so WL uses \
that executable.\n\nA minimal thing to test is whether the evaluator can see \
Python: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      RowBox[{"FindExternalEvaluators", "[", "\"Python\"", "]"}]], "ChatCode",
      "Input", LanguageCategory -> "Input", ShowAutoStyles -> True, 
     ShowStringCharacters -> True, ShowSyntaxStyles -> True, 
     TranslationOptions -> {"Enabled" -> Dynamic[
         AbsoluteCurrentValue[$FrontEnd, {TranslationOptions, "Enabled"}]]}], 
    "Wolfram"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "86eb2267-6555-410d-8d2f-3b60c770107d"],
 "\nIf needed, configure the evaluator to point to the interpreter from your ",
 StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
 " environment, then test: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"Python\"", ",", "\"2+2\""}], "]"}]], "ChatCode", "Input", 
     LanguageCategory -> "Input", ShowAutoStyles -> True, 
     ShowStringCharacters -> True, ShowSyntaxStyles -> True, 
     TranslationOptions -> {"Enabled" -> Dynamic[
         AbsoluteCurrentValue[$FrontEnd, {TranslationOptions, "Enabled"}]]}], 
    "Wolfram"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "0e7f5a52-5ff9-4381-acb8-c9e5c99d6152"],
 "\nand then: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"Python\"", ",", "\"import lpips; 'ok'\""}], "]"}]], 
     "ChatCode", "Input", LanguageCategory -> "Input", ShowAutoStyles -> True,
      ShowStringCharacters -> True, ShowSyntaxStyles -> True, 
     TranslationOptions -> {"Enabled" -> Dynamic[
         AbsoluteCurrentValue[$FrontEnd, {TranslationOptions, "Enabled"}]]}], 
    "Wolfram"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "f8138b93-1e4f-4399-9995-c852bf1f2799"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Why I still prefer Python over WL reimplementation\"\>", 
    "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"d0e41c9d-dff8-40a7-a825-d09a065a6c90"],
 "\nBecause LPIPS and similar metrics depend on: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "pretrained model weights"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"73e6d4c7-a31c-4ef0-bf3a-5526d99f50cd"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "exact preprocessing"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"e77abc33-b6a0-44ce-b700-9972705acc38"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "PyTorch semantics"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"6d639524-0779-4214-b3d6-fba4bd8f5a33"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "often GPU support"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"9b2be4ad-f297-4f7c-9ab1-476702e41a60"],
 "\nUsing the upstream Python implementation avoids mismatch. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"A nice WL-facing design\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"771e17e4-9c8d-4617-8f99-880fa608f5e2"],
 "\nI would make a small wrapper function in WL with this shape: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      RowBox[{"lpipsDistance", "[", 
        RowBox[{"image1_Image", ",", "image2_Image", ",", "opts___"}], "]"}]],
      "ChatCode", "Input", LanguageCategory -> "Input", ShowAutoStyles -> 
     True, ShowStringCharacters -> True, ShowSyntaxStyles -> True, 
     TranslationOptions -> {"Enabled" -> Dynamic[
         AbsoluteCurrentValue[$FrontEnd, {TranslationOptions, "Enabled"}]]}], 
    "Wolfram"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "9679fe43-b8fe-40ab-b5f0-255ebeeb0275"],
 "\nInternally it would:\n\n1. export images to temporary files, or convert \
to arrays\n2. ask Python to compute the metric\n3. return a WL number \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"File-based transfer is the easiest first version\"\>", 
    "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"27b4005f-bcc8-4145-abd3-68f907ea0a50"],
 "\nThis is usually the most robust start: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "WL exports images as PNG"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"2e14d3cf-1be6-4dd1-8f42-4e105eb961ff"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "Python loads them"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"606ee29c-1fec-4df2-bfc0-9ad630fb992d"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "metric is computed"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"084e279b-6f4a-4642-8fef-5eda39dfa163"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "result is returned as a scalar"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"6d70de95-a8fc-4711-ab55-c2f8066077e0"],
 "\nThat avoids early friction around: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "tensor shapes"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"5d8b61c7-14a1-4ae6-8b1e-e59eac78a48a"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "RGB channel ordering"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"5dc1a61c-3a78-454a-9649-6423f59b0b00"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "byte vs real arrays"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"ca3b5a00-2983-4143-b59a-9799b96e4cd4"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "normalization conventions"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"29088912-6d24-4217-9bdd-90aceb3ecc48"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Slightly more advanced: persistent session\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"caa478bf-031f-4cc2-b53f-ea981c02a9d9"],
 "\nIf you\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll call the metric many times, keep a persistent \
Python session alive and cache the model in memory.\n\nThat is much better \
than re-importing torch/lpips every call.\n\nConceptually: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"session", "=", 
            RowBox[{"StartExternalSession", "[", "\"Python\"", "]"}]}], ";"}],
         "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
        RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", 
          
          RowBox[{"session", ",", 
            "\"\nimport lpips\nloss_fn = lpips.LPIPS(net='alex')\n\""}], 
          "]"}]}]], "ChatCode", "Input", LanguageCategory -> "Input", 
     ShowAutoStyles -> True, ShowStringCharacters -> True, ShowSyntaxStyles -> 
     True, TranslationOptions -> {"Enabled" -> Dynamic[
         AbsoluteCurrentValue[$FrontEnd, {TranslationOptions, "Enabled"}]]}], 
    "Wolfram"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "fc9964bb-cdcc-49dc-b11d-c5c9d1d24ef2"],
 "\nThen future calls just send image paths and evaluate with the \
already-loaded ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell["loss_fn", Background -> None]},
   "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
  "dbfc91c3-6bf8-4a41-883c-8b25a23e4dc9"],
 ". \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"If you want WL to stay clean\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"b159f4d0-e235-49fe-8f1b-dade80519cac"],
 "\nA very maintainable pattern is: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "keep the Python code in a small ",
  Cell[BoxData[
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell["metrics.py", Background -> None]},
    "ChatCodeInlineTemplate"]], "ChatCodeActive",ExpressionUUID->
   "d6097da1-395f-4fc7-a096-57ff924db1b1"],
  " file in your project"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"bffb9bf3-7714-49ed-96b2-ef37ad578806"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "WL calls into that file through Python"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"84fe3656-fa62-4bff-af59-7e8a17d36fad"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "WL remains a thin orchestrator"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"44c2cc58-1ddd-4504-ab45-04be2779b684"],
 "\nThis is often nicer than embedding long Python strings in notebook cells. \
\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"If you want dependency declarations from WL\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"90f5b389-8b80-45aa-a215-7473ece217c5"],
 "\nWolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Python environment support can provision \
dependencies automatically via the evaluator\[CloseCurlyQuote]s ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Dependencies\>\""], "InlineWL", "Input",
  ShowAutoStyles->True,
  ShowSyntaxStyles->True,
  LanguageCategory->"Input",
  ShowStringCharacters->True,ExpressionUUID->
  "bff44742-2867-4c59-8bfe-ebf9341a901f"],
 " setting, including pinned versions and requirements files. For example: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", " ", 
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"\"Python\"", ",", 
              RowBox[{"\"Evaluator\"", "->", 
                RowBox[{"<|", 
                  RowBox[{"\"Dependencies\"", "->", 
                    RowBox[{"{", "\"numpy==2.2.2\"", "}"}]}], "|>"}]}]}], 
            "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", " ", 
          "\"import numpy; numpy.__version__\""}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
        "]"}]], "ChatCode", "Input", LanguageCategory -> "Input", 
     ShowAutoStyles -> True, ShowStringCharacters -> True, ShowSyntaxStyles -> 
     True, TranslationOptions -> {"Enabled" -> Dynamic[
         AbsoluteCurrentValue[$FrontEnd, {TranslationOptions, "Enabled"}]]}], 
    "Wolfram"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "35fe2098-3795-4c5f-b2d7-d04439761bc4"],
 "\nThat\[CloseCurlyQuote]s useful, but if you\[CloseCurlyQuote]re \
standardized on ",
 StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
 ", I\[CloseCurlyQuote]d only use this if you want WL to own the environment \
lifecycle. Otherwise, it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s cleaner to keep: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
  " = environment/dependency manager"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"4f776fa2-9b7f-41c6-82ac-f518f3471b94"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "WL = caller"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"dd5c4fc7-a0aa-40da-8ed4-295cb890f062"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Suggested path forward\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"3de72a18-2d31-4259-8fc9-b07dd948358c"],
 "\nI\[CloseCurlyQuote]d do this in stages: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Stage 1\"\>", "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"42bc45e9-8b0e-408b-9a7d-2fd68e358d82"],
 "\nGet WL talking to your ",
 StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
 " Python.\n\nTest: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "Python executable visible"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"9c7459a3-af31-4650-b247-2ce9af1d4d73"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  StyleBox["torch", "TI"],
  " imports"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"dc29e85e-2398-4dea-b615-539fab938329"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  StyleBox["lpips", "TI"],
  " imports"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"2968a760-20b7-4973-9adc-0a9fe7652ea7"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Stage 2\"\>", "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"72f506ff-79aa-4179-9c24-07b6092c67e1"],
 "\nImplement a tiny Python function such as: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      Cell[
      "def lpips_distance(path1, path2, net=\"alex\"):\n    ...\n    return \
float(score)", "ExternalLanguage", CellEvaluationLanguage -> "Python", 
       FontSize -> 13, Background -> None, CellFrame -> None]]], "Python"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "eb4a911a-4790-40dd-add5-70221cb44065"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Stage 3\"\>", "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"ee1417aa-b758-41ff-b32e-8c995b5badd0"],
 "\nWrap it in WL as: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     BoxData[
      RowBox[{"lpipsDistance", "[", 
        RowBox[{"img1_Image", ",", "img2_Image", ",", "opts___"}], "]"}]], 
     "ChatCode", "Input", LanguageCategory -> "Input", ShowAutoStyles -> True,
      ShowStringCharacters -> True, ShowSyntaxStyles -> True, 
     TranslationOptions -> {"Enabled" -> Dynamic[
         AbsoluteCurrentValue[$FrontEnd, {TranslationOptions, "Enabled"}]]}], 
    "Wolfram"},
   "ChatCodeBlockTemplate"]], "ChatCodeBlock",ExpressionUUID->
  "d00c05ff-09b9-4dc2-9ea1-7b2039d091e5"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"Stage 4\"\>", "Subsection",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"443b62d9-47d7-4855-bfba-9a1528e66202"],
 "\nIf needed, generalize to other metrics: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "SSIM"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"a8fbc9b1-4fd2-4118-bfea-328d96504dac"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "PSNR"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"6c378f0e-1e4f-468a-a298-ca669e41ca5f"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "DISTS"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"c807b27e-9c0e-49c2-817c-7ae10297849b"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "CLIP-based similarity"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"b90fb1c5-f21e-402b-b7f5-e05135f0f0fe"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "custom torch models"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"adef1234-049e-4225-bd5d-d6b67005db00"],
 "\nThen your WL API can become a unified metric front end. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"My opinionated choice\"\>", "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"2dcd6a49-31f1-4828-b6bf-aa224c575bac"],
 "\nIf you\[CloseCurlyQuote]re restarting this now, I would ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " begin with a WL reimplementation.\n\nI would build: \n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "one ",
  StyleBox["uv", "TI"],
  " env"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"c764338b-a371-4be1-b20c-e637ba56fc0c"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "one Python module with metric functions"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"38baee7f-66c4-4254-b715-271ac6862d55"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "one persistent WL Python session"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"4427ffb6-b287-4061-b1f8-068c20232995"],
 "\n",
 Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["\[Bullet]",
   FontColor->LightDarkSwitched[
     GrayLevel[0.5], 
     GrayLevel[0.7533742]]],
  " ",
  "one WL wrapper API"
 }], "InlineItem",ExpressionUUID->"9c7ff29b-f292-42b6-a9db-efb40f303450"],
 "\nThat gives the fastest route to something trustworthy. \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneBox[
   StyleBox["\<\"If you want, I can write you either of these next\"\>", 
    "Section",
    CellFrame->0,
    ShowStringCharacters->False,
    FontSize->22],
   ImageMargins->{{0, 0}, {5, 15}}]], "InlineSection",
  Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"034eae5b-c608-4c39-a9ec-d4a265ca94fd"],
 "\n1. a ",
 StyleBox["minimal WL + uv + Python setup checklist",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n2. a ",
 StyleBox["WL wrapper function for LPIPS",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n3. a ",
 StyleBox["small Python module",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " that WL can call for multiple image metrics\n4. a ",
 StyleBox["persistent-session design",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " that caches models in Python\n\nIf you want, I can draft the exact WL and \
Python code for option 3, which is probably the cleanest starting point."
}], "ChatOutput",
 TaggingRules-><|
  "CellToStringData" -> 
   "That\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a good fit. If you\[CloseCurlyQuote]re already \
using ``uv``, I\[CloseCurlyQuote]d still suggest a **Python-backed \
integration** from WL, with ``uv`` managing the environment and dependencies.\
\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUse:\n\n* ``uv`` to create/manage a dedicated Python \
environment\n* [ExternalEvaluate](paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate) or \
[StartExternalSession](paclet:ref/StartExternalSession) from WL\n* a small WL \
wrapper that talks to that Python environment\n\nThis gives you:\n\n* \
reproducible Python deps\n* access to PyTorch / LPIPS without \
reimplementation\n* a clean WL-facing API\n\n## Two workable patterns\n\n### \
1. Point WL at a ``uv``-managed Python\n\nThis is the simplest if your ``uv`` \
environment already has everything installed.\n\nAt the WL side, you want \
Python configured so that \
[FindExternalEvaluators](paclet:ref/FindExternalEvaluators) can see it, then \
use [ExternalEvaluate](paclet:ref/ExternalEvaluate).\n\nTypical docs flow is:\
\n\n* verify Python exists\n* install needed packages\n* confirm with \
``FindExternalEvaluators[\"Python\"]``\n* call ``ExternalEvaluate[\"Python\", \
...]``\n\nThe docs also support dependency-managed evaluators directly \
through:\n\n```wl\nExternalEvaluate[\n {\"Python\", \"Evaluator\" -> \
<|\"Dependencies\" -> {\"numpy\"}|>},\n \"import numpy; numpy.__version__\"\n\
]\n```\n\nThat dependency mechanism is useful, but since you already use \
``uv``, I would probably **let uv own the environment**, rather than split \
package management between WL and the external evaluator provisioner.\n\n## \
Best practical setup with ``uv``\n\nI\[CloseCurlyQuote]d suggest a \
project-local environment dedicated to image metrics.\n\nFor example, outside \
WL:\n\n```bash\nuv venv .venv\nuv pip install torch torchvision lpips pillow\n\
```\n\nThen identify the Python executable inside that environment, something \
like:\n\n* macOS/Linux: ``.venv/bin/python``\n* Windows: \
``.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe``\n\nThen in WL, use that interpreter \
explicitly.\n\n## How to connect WL to that Python\n\nA good first step in WL \
is to start a session with that interpreter. Depending on your setup, this \
usually means configuring Python so WL uses that executable.\n\nA minimal \
thing to test is whether the evaluator can see Python:\n\n```wl\n\
FindExternalEvaluators[\"Python\"]\n```\n\nIf needed, configure the evaluator \
to point to the interpreter from your ``uv`` environment, then test:\n\n```wl\
\nExternalEvaluate[\"Python\", \"2+2\"]\n```\n\nand then:\n\n```wl\n\
ExternalEvaluate[\"Python\", \"import lpips; 'ok'\"]\n```\n\n## Why I still \
prefer Python over WL reimplementation\n\nBecause LPIPS and similar metrics \
depend on:\n\n* pretrained model weights\n* exact preprocessing\n* PyTorch \
semantics\n* often GPU support\n\nUsing the upstream Python implementation \
avoids mismatch.\n\n## A nice WL-facing design\n\nI would make a small \
wrapper function in WL with this shape:\n\n```wl\nlpipsDistance[image1_Image, \
image2_Image, opts___]\n```\n\nInternally it would:\n\n1. export images to \
temporary files, or convert to arrays\n2. ask Python to compute the metric\n\
3. return a WL number\n\n### File-based transfer is the easiest first version\
\n\nThis is usually the most robust start:\n\n* WL exports images as PNG\n* \
Python loads them\n* metric is computed\n* result is returned as a scalar\n\n\
That avoids early friction around:\n\n* tensor shapes\n* RGB channel ordering\
\n* byte vs real arrays\n* normalization conventions\n\n## Slightly more \
advanced: persistent session\n\nIf you\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll call the metric \
many times, keep a persistent Python session alive and cache the model in \
memory.\n\nThat is much better than re-importing torch/lpips every call.\n\n\
Conceptually:\n\n```wl\nsession = StartExternalSession[\"Python\"];\n\
ExternalEvaluate[session, \"\nimport lpips\nloss_fn = lpips.LPIPS(net='alex')\
\n\"]\n```\n\nThen future calls just send image paths and evaluate with the \
already-loaded ``loss_fn``.\n\n## If you want WL to stay clean\n\nA very \
maintainable pattern is:\n\n* keep the Python code in a small ``metrics.py`` \
file in your project\n* WL calls into that file through Python\n* WL remains \
a thin orchestrator\n\nThis is often nicer than embedding long Python strings \
in notebook cells.\n\n## If you want dependency declarations from WL\n\n\
Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Python environment support can provision \
dependencies automatically via the evaluator\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
``\"Dependencies\"`` setting, including pinned versions and requirements \
files. For example:\n\n```wl\nExternalEvaluate[\n {\"Python\", \"Evaluator\" \
-> <|\"Dependencies\" -> {\"numpy==2.2.2\"}|>},\n \"import numpy; \
numpy.__version__\"\n]\n```\n\nThat\[CloseCurlyQuote]s useful, but if you\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]re standardized on ``uv``, I\[CloseCurlyQuote]d only use \
this if you want WL to own the environment lifecycle. Otherwise, it\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s cleaner to keep:\n\n* ``uv`` = environment/dependency \
manager\n* WL = caller\n\n## Suggested path forward\n\nI\[CloseCurlyQuote]d \
do this in stages:\n\n### Stage 1\nGet WL talking to your ``uv`` Python.\n\n\
Test:\n\n* Python executable visible\n* ``torch`` imports\n* ``lpips`` \
imports\n\n### Stage 2\nImplement a tiny Python function such as:\n\n\
```python\ndef lpips_distance(path1, path2, net=\"alex\"):\n    ...\n    \
return float(score)\n```\n\n### Stage 3\nWrap it in WL as:\n\n```wl\n\
lpipsDistance[img1_Image, img2_Image, opts___]\n```\n\n### Stage 4\nIf \
needed, generalize to other metrics:\n\n* SSIM\n* PSNR\n* DISTS\n* CLIP-based \
similarity\n* custom torch models\n\nThen your WL API can become a unified \
metric front end.\n\n## My opinionated choice\n\nIf you\[CloseCurlyQuote]re \
restarting this now, I would **not** begin with a WL reimplementation.\n\nI \
would build:\n\n* one ``uv`` env\n* one Python module with metric functions\n\
* one persistent WL Python session\n* one WL wrapper API\n\nThat gives the \
fastest route to something trustworthy.\n\n## If you want, I can write you \
either of these next\n\n1. a **minimal WL + uv + Python setup checklist**\n2. \
a **WL wrapper function for LPIPS**\n3. a **small Python module** that WL can \
call for multiple image metrics\n4. a **persistent-session design** that \
caches models in Python\n\nIf you want, I can draft the exact WL and Python \
code for option 3, which is probably the cleanest starting point.", 
